'''Season thirty-four''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' premiered on [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] and [[Disney+]] on September 16, 2025, and concluded on December 2, 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Schwartz |first1=Ryan |date=July 17, 2025 |title=ABC Sets Fall Premiere Dates for ''9-1-1: Nashville,'' ''High Potential'', ''Grey's'' and More — Most Scripted Shows Held for October |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/abc-fall-tv-premiere-dates-2025-911-greys-anatomy-1235466281/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250717182039/https://tvline.com/news/abc-fall-tv-premiere-dates-2025-911-greys-anatomy-1235466281/ |archive-date=July 17, 2025 |access-date=July 17, 2025 |website=[[TVLine]] |language=en-US}}</ref> This season, marking the twentieth anniversary of the series, was the third to air live on both networks simultaneously and the first of ABC's unscripted programs to earn an official renewal for their [[2025–26 United States network television schedule|2025–26 schedule]].<ref name="RenewalTHR">{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=April 22, 2025 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Renewed for Season 34, Reveals First Contestant |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-renewed-season-34-robert-irwin-1236198199/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250424035841/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-renewed-season-34-robert-irwin-1236198199/ |archive-date=April 24, 2025 |access-date=May 22, 2025 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 19|Season nineteen]] champion [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] returned to host the installment, while former professional dancer and judge [[Julianne Hough]] returned as co-host.<ref>{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Renewed for Season 34 and Reveals First Celebrity Cast Member |date=April 22, 2025 |publisher=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |url=https://www.dgepress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-renewed-for-season-34-and-reveals-first-celebrity-cast-member/ |via=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |access-date=May 22, 2025 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250423042242/https://www.dgepress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-renewed-for-season-34-and-reveals-first-celebrity-cast-member/ |archive-date=April 23, 2025}}</ref>

Wildlife conservationist [[Robert Irwin]] and [[Witney Carson]] were crowned the champions, while social media personality [[Alix Earle]] and [[Val Chmerkovskiy]] finished in second place, Olympic artistic gymnast [[Jordan Chiles]] and [[Ezra Sosa]] finished third, reality television personality [[Dylan Efron]] and [[Daniella Karagach]] finished fourth, and actress [[Elaine Hendrix]] and [[Alan Bersten]] finished fifth. A holiday television special aired following the season finale.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Petski |first=Denise |date=November 4, 2025 |title=ABC Sets Holiday Programming Including Kevin Costner, ''CMA Country Christmas'' & ''Dancing With The Stars'' Specials, Returning ''Home Alone'', NBA & More |url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/abc-holiday-schedule-2025-dancing-with-the-stars-1236606758/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251119130814/https://deadline.com/2025/11/abc-holiday-schedule-2025-dancing-with-the-stars-1236606758/ |archive-date=November 19, 2025 |access-date=December 3, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

== Cast ==
=== Couples ===
On April 22, 2025, during an [[Upfront (advertising)|upfront]] for [[Hulu]]'s unscripted programming, [[Robert Irwin]] was announced as the first celebrity participant for the thirty-fourth season.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bernabe |first=Angeline Jane |date=April 22, 2025 |title=Robert Irwin joins ''Dancing with the Stars'' season 34 |url=https://www.goodmorningamerica.com/culture/story/robert-irwin-joins-dancing-stars-season-34-121033493 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250423034204/https://www.goodmorningamerica.com/culture/story/robert-irwin-joins-dancing-stars-season-34-121033493 |archive-date=April 23, 2025 |access-date=May 29, 2025 |website=[[Good Morning America]] |language=en}}</ref> He is the younger brother of [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 21|season twenty-one]] winner, [[Bindi Irwin]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Seemayer |first=Zach |date=May 5, 2019 |title=Steve Irwin's Lookalike Son Robert Wants to Be on ''Dancing With the Stars'' (Exclusive) |url=https://www.etonline.com/steve-irwins-lookalike-son-robert-wants-to-be-on-dancing-with-the-stars-exclusive-124650 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190515125959/https://www.etonline.com/steve-irwins-lookalike-son-robert-wants-to-be-on-dancing-with-the-stars-exclusive-124650 |archive-date=May 15, 2019 |access-date=May 29, 2025 |website=[[Entertainment Tonight]] |language=en-US}}</ref> [[Alix Earle]] joined the cast one month later.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Longeretta |first=Emily |date=May 22, 2025 |title=Influencer Alix Earle Joins ''Dancing With the Stars'' Season 34 |url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/alix-earle-dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-1236406474/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250522125525/https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/alix-earle-dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-1236406474/ |archive-date=May 22, 2025 |access-date=May 22, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US}}</ref> On June 30, during ''[[The Secret Lives of Mormon Wives]]''<nowiki/>' second season reunion special,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Fell |first=Nicole |date=June 30, 2025 |title=''Secret Lives of Mormon Wives'' Reunion Surprise: Jen Affleck and Whitney Leavitt Joining ''Dancing With the Stars'' |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/the-secret-lives-of-mormon-wives-reunion-dwts-1236303413/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701070639/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/the-secret-lives-of-mormon-wives-reunion-dwts-1236303413/ |archive-date=July 1, 2025 |access-date=July 1, 2025 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> host [[Nick Viall]] revealed that [[Jen Affleck]] and [[Whitney Leavitt]] were joining ''Dancing with the Stars''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Patton |first=Tess |date=July 1, 2025 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Taps 2 ''Mormon Wives'' Stars for Season 34 |url=https://www.thewrap.com/dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-cast-mormon-wives-jen-affleck-whitney-leavitt/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701142549/https://www.thewrap.com/dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-cast-mormon-wives-jen-affleck-whitney-leavitt/ |archive-date=July 1, 2025 |access-date=July 1, 2025 |website=[[TheWrap]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Affleck announced the birth of her third child two days later;<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Edel |first1=Victoria |last2=Sacks |first2=Hannah |date=July 2, 2025 |title=''Mormon Wives''{{'}} Jen Affleck Welcomes Her Third Baby with Husband Zac: 'So Grateful and So Happy' |url=https://people.com/jennifer-affleck-baby-no-3-zac-affleck-11737877 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250702225434/https://people.com/jennifer-affleck-baby-no-3-zac-affleck-11737877 |archive-date=July 2, 2025 |access-date=September 2, 2025 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]] |language=en}}</ref> she was eight weeks [[Postpartum period|postpartum]] when the season premiered.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Norwin |first=Alyssa |date=August 31, 2025 |title=Why Jen Affleck Is 'Looking Forward' to Doing ''DWTS'' 2 Months Postpartum |url=https://www.tvinsider.com/1211934/dancing-with-the-stars-jennifer-affleck-interview-postpartum-baby/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250903140650/https://www.tvinsider.com/1211934/dancing-with-the-stars-jennifer-affleck-interview-postpartum-baby/ |archive-date=September 3, 2025 |access-date=September 1, 2025 |website=TV Insider |language=en-US}}</ref> On August 25, ''[[Entertainment Tonight]]'' reported that [[Hilaria Baldwin]] joined the cast; ''[[People (magazine)|People]]'' confirmed her appearance the following day.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Moore |first=Julia |date=August 26, 2025 |title=Hilaria Baldwin Is Expected to Compete on ''Dancing with the Stars'' Season 34 |url=https://people.com/hilaria-baldwin-is-expected-to-compete-on-dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-11797606 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/k2bsw |archive-date=March 24, 2026 |access-date=August 27, 2025 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Jordon Hudson]] was originally cast to compete on the season, but she declined due to [[Conflict of interest|conflicts of interest]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Trainor |first=Daniel |date=September 18, 2025 |title=Why Jordon Hudson's ''Dancing With the Stars'' Casting Really 'Fell Apart': Source (Exclusive) |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/why-jordon-hudsons-dancing-with-the-stars-casting-really-fell-apart-excl/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251008183349/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/why-jordon-hudsons-dancing-with-the-stars-casting-really-fell-apart-excl/ |archive-date=October 8, 2025 |access-date=October 2, 2025 |website=[[Us Weekly]] |language=en-US}}</ref> The full roster of celebrity participants and their partnerships was officially revealed on ''[[Good Morning America]]'' on September 3.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rice |first=Lynette |date=September 3, 2025 |title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Cast Reveal: Hilaria Baldwin, Andy Richter & Corey Feldman To Compete In Season 34 |url=https://deadline.com/2025/09/dancing-with-the-stars-cast-reveal-season-34-2025-1236504833/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250910142608/https://deadline.com/2025/09/dancing-with-the-stars-cast-reveal-season-34-2025-1236504833/ |archive-date=September 10, 2025 |access-date=September 3, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name="TFC-PR cast">{{cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Cha-Chas Back to the Ballroom with an All-New Celebrity Cast |date=September 3, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2025/09/03/dancing-with-the-stars-cha-chas-back-to-the-ballroom-with-an-all-new-celebrity-cast-822011/20250903abc01/ |via=[[The Futon Critic]] |access-date=September 3, 2025 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/blQ9G |archive-date=March 24, 2026}}</ref>

According to ''[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]]'', [[Artem Chigvintsev]] was not slated to return as a professional dancer this season.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Jakiel |first1=Olivia |last2=Brody |first2=Lanae |date=July 16, 2025 |title=Source Reveals If Artem Chigvintsev Is Slated to Return to ''DWTS'' This Season (Exclusive) |url=https://parade.com/tv/artem-chigvintsev-return-dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-exclusive |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250716212222/https://parade.com/tv/artem-chigvintsev-return-dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-exclusive |archive-date=July 16, 2025 |access-date=July 19, 2025 |website=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]] |language=en}}</ref> Entertainment journalist Kristyn Burtt announced that [[Mark Ballas]],<ref name="BallasReturn">{{Cite web |last=Carey |first=Stacy |date=August 18, 2025 |title=Beloved Retired ''DWTS'' Pro's Possible Season 34 Comeback Has Fans Buzzing |url=https://parade.com/news/beloved-retired-dwts-pros-possible-season-34-comeback-has-fans-buzzing |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250823152516/https://parade.com/news/beloved-retired-dwts-pros-possible-season-34-comeback-has-fans-buzzing |archive-date=August 23, 2025 |access-date=August 19, 2025 |website=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Britt Stewart]], [[Brandon Armstrong (dancer)|Brandon Armstrong]], [[Rylee Arnold]], [[Ezra Sosa]], [[Emma Slater]], [[Valentin Chmerkovskiy]], [[Daniella Karagach]], [[Pasha Pashkov]], [[Alan Bersten]], [[Witney Carson]], [[Gleb Savchenko]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galante |first=Grace |date=August 22, 2025 |title=''DWTS'' Fans Upset After Controversial Pro Is Rumored to Return for Season 34 |url=https://parade.com/news/dwts-fans-upset-controversial-pro-gleb-savchenko-rumored-return-season-34 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250823185256/https://parade.com/news/dwts-fans-upset-controversial-pro-gleb-savchenko-rumored-return-season-34 |archive-date=August 23, 2025 |access-date=August 25, 2025 |website=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]] |language=en}}</ref> and the reigning champion [[Jenna Johnson (dancer)|Jenna Johnson]] were slated to return.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Galante |first=Grace |date=August 27, 2025 |title=Carrie Ann Inaba Seemingly Confirms Pro Lineup for ''DWTS'' Season 34 |url=https://parade.com/news/carrie-ann-inaba-confirms-pro-lineup-dwts-season-34 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250827205226/https://parade.com/news/carrie-ann-inaba-confirms-pro-lineup-dwts-season-34 |archive-date=August 27, 2025 |access-date=August 28, 2025 |website=[[Parade (magazine)|Parade]] |language=en}}</ref> Ballas competed for the first time since winning the thirty-first season with [[Charli D'Amelio]].<ref name="BallasReturn" /> Before his appearance was confirmed, Savchenko said he was not cast to return to ''Dancing with the Stars'' amid [[Infidelity|cheating]] allegations from his ex-girlfriend and [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 33|season thirty-three]] partner, [[Brooks Nader]].<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Goldberg |first1=Madison E. |last2=Blackwelder |first2=Carson |date=August 12, 2025 |title=Gleb Savchenko Says He Wasn't Invited Back to ''Dancing with the Stars'', Implies It Is Because of Brooks Nader's 'Lie' |url=https://people.com/gleb-savchenko-says-he-wasnt-invited-back-to-dwts-implies-brooks-naders-lie-11789199 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/Ng0V3 |archive-date=March 24, 2026 |access-date=August 12, 2025 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]] |language=en}}</ref> [[Jan Ravnik]], former backup dancer for [[Taylor Swift]]'s [[The Eras Tour|Eras Tour]], joined the series as a first-time pro.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=August 28, 2025 |title=Eras Tour Dancer Jan Ravnik Joins ''Dancing With the Stars'' |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-jan-ravnik-eras-tour-pro-1236355383/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250828133746/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-jan-ravnik-eras-tour-pro-1236355383/ |archive-date=August 28, 2025 |access-date=August 28, 2025 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> Although [[Sasha Farber]] did not return as a pro this season, he was involved in other capacities.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Blackwelder |first=Carson |date=September 16, 2025 |title=Sasha Farber Will Still Be Involved in ''Dancing with the Stars'' Season 34 Despite Not Competing as a Pro: Find Out How! |url=https://people.com/sasha-farber-will-still-be-involved-dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-11811119 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250924161937/https://people.com/sasha-farber-will-still-be-involved-dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-11811119 |archive-date=September 24, 2025 |access-date=September 16, 2025 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

