Each couple performed one unlearned dance to a "personal anthem" of the celebrity.<ref name="Week1BB">{{Cite magazine |last=Chan |first=Anna |date=September 10, 2025 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Competitors to Groove to Music From Ariana Grande, ''KPop Demon Hunters'' & More in Premiere |url=https://www.billboard.com/culture/tv-film/ariana-grande-kpop-demon-hunters-music-dwts-season-premiere-1236063694/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250911015754/https://www.billboard.com/culture/tv-film/ariana-grande-kpop-demon-hunters-music-dwts-season-premiere-1236063694/ |archive-date=September 11, 2025 |access-date=September 10, 2025 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |language=en-US}}</ref> There was no elimination this week; all scores were carried over to the following week.<ref name="Week1PR" /> [[Carrie Ann Inaba]] missed this episode due to an undisclosed illness, so the couples were judged on a 20-point scale instead of the usual 30-point scale.<ref name="InabaPremiere" /> The [[Number (music)|opening number]], choreographed by Ray Leeper, was set to "[[Kill the Lights (Alex Newell, DJ Cassidy and Nile Rodgers song)|Kill the Lights]]" by Whitney Myer.<ref name="Week1PR" /> The troupe also performed a number to "[[Just Keep Watching]]" by [[Tate McRae]].<ref name="Week1PR" />

