Each couple performed one unlearned dance to a song by a [[one-hit wonder]].<ref name="Week2PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Brings Chart-Toppers to the Ballroom on 'One-Hit Wonders Night' Sept. 23 |date=September 17, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-chart-toppers-to-the-ballroom-on-one-hit-wonders-night-sept-23/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=September 17, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250918012553/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-brings-chart-toppers-to-the-ballroom-on-one-hit-wonders-night-sept-23/ |archive-date=September 18, 2025}}</ref> A double elimination took place this week.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rice |first=Lynette |date=September 16, 2025 |title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Season Premiere: Find Out Who Performed A Cheeky Cha Cha & Admitted He Was In It For The Paycheck |url=https://deadline.com/2025/09/dancing-with-the-stars-season-premiere-who-went-home-1236546327/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250917022350/https://deadline.com/2025/09/dancing-with-the-stars-season-premiere-who-went-home-1236546327/ |archive-date=September 17, 2025 |access-date=September 17, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US}}</ref> The opening number, choreographed by [[Emma Slater]], was set to "[[Gonna Make You Sweat (Everybody Dance Now)]]" by [[C+C Music Factory]] feat. [[Freedom Williams]].<ref name="Week2PR" /> The troupe also performed numbers to "[[I Like to Move It]]" by [[Reel 2 Real]] feat. [[the Mad Stuntman]] and "[[Lady (Hear Me Tonight)]]" by [[Modjo]].<ref name="Week2PR" />

