=== Week 3: TikTok Night ===
Each couple performed one unlearned dance to a song that went [[Viral phenomenon|viral]] on the social media platform [[TikTok]].<ref name="Week3PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' is Trending on 'TikTok Night' Sept. 30 |date=September 26, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-is-trending-on-tiktok-night-sept-30/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=September 26, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251001025750/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-is-trending-on-tiktok-night-sept-30/ |archive-date=October 1, 2025}}</ref> The opening number was set to "[[Apple (song)|Apple]]" by [[Charli XCX]] and featured [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 31|season 31]] champion [[Charli D'Amelio]], with [[Apple (song)#Recognition and cover versions|viral moves]] created by actor and content creator Kelley Heyer.<ref name="Week3PR" /> The troupe performed a number to "[[No Broke Boys]]" by [[Disco Lines]] and [[Tinashe]].<ref name="Week3PR" /> They also performed a number with D'Amelio to "[[Savage (Megan Thee Stallion song)|Savage]]" by [[Megan Thee Stallion]], choreographed by [[Jenna Johnson (dancer)|Jenna Johnson Chmerkovskiy]] and [[Britt Stewart]] with viral moves created by content creator Keke Janajah.<ref name="Week3PR" /> D'Amelio also performed with her season 31 pro partner [[Mark Ballas]] to "[[Assumptions (song)|Assumptions]]" by [[Sam Gellaitry]].<ref name="Week3PR" />

