=== Week 4: Disney Night ===
To celebrate the seventieth anniversary of [[Disneyland]], each couple performed one unlearned dance to a song inspired by a [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] film or attraction.<ref name="Week4PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Celebrates the Magic on 'Disney Night' Oct. 7 |date=October 1, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-celebrates-the-magic-on-disney-night-oct-7/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=October 1, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251006153043/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-celebrates-the-magic-on-disney-night-oct-7/ |archive-date=October 6, 2025}}</ref> The opening number, choreographed by [[Mandy Moore (choreographer)|Mandy Moore]], was set to "[[Be Our Guest]]" from ''[[Beauty and the Beast (1991 film)|Beauty and the Beast]]'' (1991) and featured a guest appearance from Danny Gardner, who stars as [[List of Disney's Beauty and the Beast characters#Lumière|Lumière]] on the North American tour of its [[Beauty and the Beast (musical)|accompanying stage musical]].<ref name="Week4PR" /> The troupe performed numbers to "[[As Alive as You Need Me to Be]]" from ''[[Tron: Ares]]'' (2025) and "The Tiki Tiki Room" from [[Walt Disney's Enchanted Tiki Room]].<ref name="Week4PR" />

