''Individual judges' scores in the charts below (given in parentheses) are listed in this order from left to right: Carrie Ann Inaba, Derek Hough, [[Jon M. Chu]], Bruno Tonioli.''

Each couple performed one unlearned dance to a song from either the [[Musical film|musical]] [[fantasy film]] ''[[Wicked (2024 film)|Wicked]]'' (2024) or its then-upcoming sequel, ''[[Wicked: For Good]]'' (2025).<ref name="Week6PR">{{Cite press release |title=The ''Dancing with the Stars'' Ballroom Transforms Into Emerald City for {{'}}''Wicked'' Night' Oct. 21 |date=October 16, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/the-dancing-with-the-stars-ballroom-transforms-into-emerald-city-for-wicked-night-oct-21/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=October 16, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251016200913/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/the-dancing-with-the-stars-ballroom-transforms-into-emerald-city-for-wicked-night-oct-21/ |archive-date=October 16, 2025}}</ref> [[Jon M. Chu]], who directed both films, appeared as a guest judge.<ref name="Week6Judge" /> The episode featured a never-before-seen clip from ''Wicked: For Good'' as well as video messages from its cast, including [[Cynthia Erivo]], [[Ariana Grande]], [[Jonathan Bailey]] and [[Michelle Yeoh]].<ref name="Week6PR" /> The opening number, choreographed by Christopher Scott, was set to a [[Medley (music)|medley]] of songs from both films: "No One Mourns the Wicked", "[[Defying Gravity (song)|Defying Gravity]]", "[[For Good]]", "Thank Goodness", "Dancing Through Life", and "What Is This Feeling?". The troupe also performed a number to "Wonderful" from ''Wicked: For Good''.<ref name="Week6PR" />

