=== Week 8: Rock & Roll Hall of Fame Night ===
''Individual judges' scores in the charts below (given in parentheses) are listed in this order from left to right: Carrie Ann Inaba, Derek Hough, [[Flavor Flav]], Bruno Tonioli.''

Each couple performed one unlearned dance to a song by an artist or group who was either [[List of Rock and Roll Hall of Fame inductees|inducted]] into the [[Rock and Roll Hall of Fame]] (RRHOF) or are slated to be.<ref name="Week8USA" /> They also participated in a team dance, which featured live performances from RRHOF inductees [[Kool & the Gang]] and [[Chicago (band)|Chicago]].<ref name="Week8PR">{{Cite press release |title=It's Time to Jam Out with the AMP Out! 'Rock & Roll Hall of Fame Night' Cranks Up the Volume on Nov. 4 |date=October 29, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/its-time-to-jam-out-with-the-amp-out-rock-roll-hall-of-fame-night-cranks-up-the-volume-on-nov-4/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=October 29, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251103002530/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/its-time-to-jam-out-with-the-amp-out-rock-roll-hall-of-fame-night-cranks-up-the-volume-on-nov-4/ |archive-date=November 3, 2025}}</ref> Rapper and television personality [[Flavor Flav]], who is also a RRHOF inductee, appeared as a guest judge.<ref name="Week8USA" />

The teams were chosen by the celebrities with the lowest combined scores, Andy and Danielle.<ref name="Week8PR" /> A [[plot twist]] was also involved; co-hosts [[Alfonso Ribeiro]] and [[Julianne Hough]] each joined a team for their dance.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rice |first=Lynette |date=October 28, 2025 |title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Week 7: Injured Elaine Hendrix Scares Up Great Scores While A Reality Star Is Sent Packing |url=https://deadline.com/2025/10/dancing-with-the-stars-week-7-1236600977/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251029023330/https://deadline.com/2025/10/dancing-with-the-stars-week-7-1236600977/ |archive-date=October 29, 2025 |access-date=October 29, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US}}</ref> The opening number, choreographed by [[Britt Stewart]], was set to "[[Pour Some Sugar on Me]]" by [[Def Leppard]] and "[[Fight the Power (Public Enemy song)|Fight the Power]]" by [[Public Enemy]].<ref name="Week8PR" /> The professional dancers who joined the ''Dancing with the Stars: Live!'' tour in 2026 performed a routine to "[[Hey Ya!]]" by [[Outkast]], choreographed by [[Mandy Moore (choreographer)|Mandy Moore]].<ref name="Week8PR" /> The troupe was originally slated to perform a number to "[[Higher Ground (Stevie Wonder song)|Higher Ground]]" by [[Stevie Wonder]],<ref name="Week8PR" /> but they instead performed to "[[I Love L.A.]]" by [[Randy Newman]] to celebrate the [[Los Angeles Dodgers]] winning the [[2025 World Series]].<ref>{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' celebrates World Series win with Dodgers tribute performance |date=November 5, 2025 |publisher=[[KABC-TV|ABC7 Los Angeles]] |url=https://abc7.com/post/dancing-stars-celebrates-world-series-win-dodgers-tribute-performance/18115055/ |via=[[The Walt Disney Company]] |access-date=November 6, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251105062556/https://abc7.com/post/dancing-stars-celebrates-world-series-win-dodgers-tribute-performance/18115055/ |archive-date=November 5, 2025}}</ref>

