=== Week 9: 20th Birthday Party ===
''Individual judges' scores in the charts below (given in parentheses) are listed in this order from left to right: Carrie Ann Inaba, Derek Hough, [[Tom Bergeron]], Bruno Tonioli.''

In celebration of the twentieth anniversary of ''Dancing with the Stars'',<ref name="Week9Deadline">{{Cite web |last=Campione |first=Katie |date=November 5, 2025 |title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Unveils Dance Styles & Songs For 20th Anniversary Celebration, Plus A New Relay Round Twist |url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/dancing-with-the-stars-20th-anniversary-dances-songs-twist-1236608397/ |access-date=November 5, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251105223510/https://deadline.com/2025/11/dancing-with-the-stars-20th-anniversary-dances-songs-twist-1236608397/|archive-date=November 5, 2025|url-status=live}}</ref> each couple reinterpreted a memorable [[Street dance|freestyle]] performance by showcasing an unlearned dance style.<ref name="Week9PR">{{Cite press release |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Celebrates Two Decades of Mirrorball Moments with a Special '20th Birthday Party' Airing Nov. 11 |date=November 5, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-celebrates-two-decades-of-mirrorball-moments-with-a-special-20th-birthday-party-airing-nov-11/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=November 5, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260324203110/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/dancing-with-the-stars-celebrates-two-decades-of-mirrorball-moments-with-a-special-20th-birthday-party-airing-nov-11/ |archive-date=March 24, 2026}}</ref> Six couples also participated in a dance relay, featuring the [[quickstep]], [[Viennese waltz]] and [[Jive (dance)|jive]], for two bonus points.<ref name="Week9Deadline" /> The dance relays featured a special twist to commemorate the milestone; for the first time ever, celebrities danced without their professional partners, instead joining forces with a returning mirrorball champion.<ref name="Champions">{{Cite web |last=Simpson |first=Kaitlin |date=November 7, 2025 |title=Which ''Dancing With the Stars'' Alums Are Returning for 20th Anniversary Episode? |url=https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/which-dancing-with-the-stars-alums-will-return-for-20th-anniversary/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251106211211/https://www.usmagazine.com/entertainment/news/which-dancing-with-the-stars-alums-will-return-for-20th-anniversary/ |archive-date=November 6, 2025 |access-date=November 5, 2025 |website=[[US Weekly]] |language=en-US}}</ref> For receiving the highest cumulative points in the season so far, Whitney & Mark earned immunity from the dance relays and automatically received two bonus points.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Tracy |first1=Brianne |last2=Kratofil |first2=Colleen |date=November 4, 2025 |title=''Dancing with the Stars'' Full Recap: Carrie Ann Apologizes to 1 Contestant as Another Breaks Down in Tears |url=https://people.com/dancing-with-the-stars-rock-roll-night-live-updates-11843415 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/mGCKJ |archive-date=March 24, 2026 |access-date=November 5, 2025 |website=[[People (magazine)|People]] |language=en}}</ref>

[[Tom Bergeron]], who hosted ''Dancing with the Stars'' for its first twenty-eight seasons, appeared as a guest judge.<ref name="Week9Judge" /> The opening number, choreographed by [[Derek Hough]], was set to a reimagined version of the "''Dancing with the Stars'' Theme" by [[Ray Chew]].<ref name="Week9PR" /> It featured the current lineup of professional dancers and troupe members, as well as the six original pros from the [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 1|first season]]: [[Alec Mazo]], [[Ashly DelGrosso]], [[Louis van Amstel]], [[Jonathan Roberts (dancer)|Jonathan Roberts]], [[Charlotte Jørgensen]], and [[Edyta Śliwińska]].<ref name="Week9PR" /> The episode also held an [[in memoriam segment]] with a routine to "[[Always Remember Us This Way]]" by [[Lady Gaga]], choreographed and performed by [[Ezra Sosa]] and [[Rylee Arnold]].<ref name="Week9PR" />

