=== Week 11: Finale ===
For the three-hour finale, each couple performed three dances: an unlearned dance selected and coached by one of the judges, an instant dance, and their [[Street dance|freestyle]] routine.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Franklin |first=McKinley |date=November 18, 2025 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Honors Prince as a Top Scoring Couple Exits Ahead of Next Week's Finale: See the Scores, Who Went Home |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dwts-prince-semi-finals-season-34-episode-10-scores-elimination-1236430355/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251119012311/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dwts-prince-semi-finals-season-34-episode-10-scores-elimination-1236430355/ |archive-date=November 19, 2025 |access-date=November 19, 2025 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> For the instant dance round, the couples had approximately five minutes to choreograph and learn a new dance before performing it live.<ref name="Week11PR">{{Cite press release |title=Live From Hollywood, It's the Season 34 Finale of ''Dancing with the Stars'' on ABC and Disney+ |date=November 20, 2025 |publisher=[[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] |url=https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/live-from-hollywood-its-the-season-34-finale-of-dancing-with-the-stars-on-abc-and-disney/ |via=[[Disney General Entertainment Content Press]] |access-date=November 20, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251124022413/https://www.detpress.com/abc/pressrelease/live-from-hollywood-its-the-season-34-finale-of-dancing-with-the-stars-on-abc-and-disney/ |archive-date=November 24, 2025}}</ref> Although the assigned dance styles and songs were not known beforehand by the couples, they were told that it would be one of four dance styles they had performed earlier in the season.<ref name="Week11PR" />

The opening number, choreographed by Joey Pizzi, was set to "[[Never Can Say Goodbye#The Communards version|Never Can Say Goodbye]]" by [[the Communards]].<ref name="Week11PR" /> All of the eliminated couples returned to the ballroom with additional performances to "[[Sugar on My Tongue]]" by [[Tyler, the Creator|Tyler]], [[Tyler, the Creator|the Creator]], "[[Applause (Lady Gaga song)|Applause]]" by [[Lady Gaga]], and "I Don't Dance" by [[Alexander Jean]].<ref name="Week11PR" /> The professional dancers featured on the ''Dancing with the Stars: Live!'' tour in 2026 performed a routine to "[[Sapphire (song)|Sapphire]]" by [[Ed Sheeran]], choreographed by [[Mandy Moore (choreographer)|Mandy Moore]].<ref name="Week11PR" /> Additional troupe and pro performances were set to "[[Talk Talk (Charli XCX song)|Talk Talk]]" by [[Charli XCX]] featuring [[Troye Sivan]] and "[[The Fate of Ophelia|The Fate of Ophelia (Alone in My Tower Acoustic Version)]]" by [[Taylor Swift]].<ref name="Week11PR" /> [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 33|Season 33]] champions [[Joey Graziadei]] and [[Jenna Johnson (dancer)|Jenna Johnson]] returned for a performance to "Tanguera" by Fabio Hager Sexteto.<ref name="Week11PR" />

