==Reception==
Season thirty-four became the program's most-watched in several years.<ref name="THR Oct 24">{{cite magazine |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=October 24, 2025 |title=TV Ratings: ''DWTS'' and ''High Potential'' Continue Strong Runs, ''Task'' Finale Scores |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-tv-ratings-momentum-2025-1236409621/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251028180849/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-tv-ratings-momentum-2025-1236409621/ |archive-date=October 28, 2025 |access-date=October 26, 2025 |magazine=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> "TikTok Night" marked the first time in twenty years that ''Dancing with the Stars'' saw an increase in viewership for two consecutive weeks since its premiere episode.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Rice |first1=Lynette |title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Logs Season High Ratings In Adult Demo, Viewers |url=https://deadline.com/2025/10/dancing-with-the-stars-logs-season-high-ratings-1236569506/ |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |date=October 3, 2025 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20251003175616/https://deadline.com/2025/10/dancing-with-the-stars-logs-season-high-ratings-1236569506/ |archive-date=October 3, 2025 |access-date=October 4, 2025}}</ref> With "''Wicked'' Night", the series became the first American fall television program in at least 34 years to increase in viewers for five weeks after its premiere episode.<ref name="THR Oct 24"/>

"Prince Night" became the show's most-watched semifinals episode in seven years.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Longeretta |first=Emily |date=November 20, 2025 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Ratings: Prince Night Hits Season High, Becomes Most Watched Semifinals in 7 Years (EXCLUSIVE) |url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-ratings-prince-night-semifinals-1236587456/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20251121040048/https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-ratings-prince-night-semifinals-1236587456/ |archive-date=November 21, 2025 |access-date=November 20, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US}}</ref> The season finale, which crowned [[Robert Irwin]] and [[Witney Carson]] as champions, became the show's highest-rated finale since [[Laurie Hernandez]] and [[Valentin Chmerkovskiy|Val Chmerkovskiy]] won in [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 23|season twenty-three]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=White |first=Peter |date=November 26, 2025 |title=''Dancing With The Stars'' Waltzes Off With Highest-Rated Finale Since 2016 |url=https://deadline.com/2025/11/dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-finale-ratings-1236629921/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20251126225312/https://deadline.com/2025/11/dancing-with-the-stars-season-34-finale-ratings-1236629921/ |archive-date=November 26, 2025 |access-date=November 26, 2025 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]] |language=en-US}}</ref> It also earned the program's strongest finale demo number since Irwin's older sister, [[Bindi Irwin|Bindi]], won with [[Derek Hough]] in [[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series) season 21|season twenty-one]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Longeretta |first=Emily |date=November 26, 2025 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'': Robert Irwin's Big Win Becomes Highest-Rated Finale Since His Sister Bindi Took Home the Mirrorball in 2015 |url=https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-finale-ratings-season-34-1236593243/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20251126230039/https://variety.com/2025/tv/news/dancing-with-the-stars-finale-ratings-season-34-1236593243/ |archive-date=November 26, 2025 |access-date=November 26, 2025 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |language=en-US}}</ref> 

Season thirty-four ended the [[2025–26 United States network television schedule|2025–26 schedule]] as the twelfth most-watched series across network television, and the twenty-fourth most-watched show overall, with an average of 9.8 million viewers.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=May 28, 2026 |title=Netflix and CBS Dominate Multi-Platform Ratings for 2025-26 Season |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/netflix-and-cbs-dominate-multi-platform-ratings-for-2025-26-season-1236607865/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260529060632/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/netflix-and-cbs-dominate-multi-platform-ratings-for-2025-26-season-1236607865/ |archive-date=May 29, 2026 |access-date=June 2, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref> At the [[78th Primetime Emmy Awards]], season thirty-four became ''Dancing with the Stars''<nowiki/>' first installment in ten years to earn a nomination for [[Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Reality Competition Program|Outstanding Reality Competition Program]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Franklin |first=McKinley |date=July 8, 2026 |title=''Dancing With the Stars'' Scores First Reality Competition Emmy Nomination in a Decade |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/dancing-with-the-stars-emmy-nomination-2026-reality-tv-1236641509/ |access-date=July 8, 2026 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]] |language=en-US}}</ref>

